<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Ortiz says 112,000 new jobs in Jan, Feb.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Ortiz says 112,000 new jobs in Jan, Feb.</headline>
<dateline>CANCUN, Mexico 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican Finance Minister Guillermo Ortiz said Friday that the country had created 112,000 new jobs in January and February, according to social security data.</p>
<p>Speaking at the annual Mexican Bankers' Convention, he added that the country's public debt levels were fully manageable.</p>
<p>&quot;We have today a public debt which in its structure and its level is fully manageable,&quot; Ortiz told attendees.</p>
<p>Ortiz said he expected Mexico's gross domestic product to grow by &quot;at least&quot; 4 percent this year. The performance of the economy so far this year allowed him to make the prediction, he said.</p>
<p>((--Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 7287902))</p>
